homelab-database (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix bootstrap-app-role.sh: it previously created its own
    "--schema" via CREATE SCHEMA ... AUTHORIZATION before applying
    --schema-sql, which silently split from whatever schema name the
    SQL file itself hardcoded internally (e.g. borg-backup-client's
    schema.sql creates `service_backup` itself) -- the role ended up
    granted on an empty, unrelated schema. Now applies --schema-sql
    as-is and only grants afterward; --schema must name what the file
    itself creates. Also added the missing `GRANT USAGE, CREATE ON
    SCHEMA` (table/sequence grants alone aren't enough to see objects
    in a schema at all) and fixed log/psql output leaking into the
    captured SCRAM_SECRET on stdout. Found and fixed via live testing
    on ssh test.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:12:41 -0500

homelab-database (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Create a shared `homelab` database on every configure (idempotent),
    as the substrate other homelab-* packages' own schemas live inside.
  * Add scripts/bootstrap-app-role.sh: a reusable tool for other
    packages' installers to create their own narrow role + schema,
    using OS-level peer auth only (local `sudo -u postgres`, or the
    same over SSH to a remote DB host, or printed SQL for a human to
    run by hand as a last resort) -- never a stored/network admin
    Postgres credential. Prints the new role's password and its
    ready-to-use SCRAM secret (from pg_authid.rolpassword) for the
    caller to use and, if applicable, register with homelab-pgbouncer.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:00:00 -0500

homelab-database (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Generic PostgreSQL provisioning/hardening substrate:
    drop-in conf.d/pg_hba.conf.d config only (never edits vendor files
    directly beyond a single idempotent, sentinel-guarded `include_dir`
    activation line), adopt-existing-cluster detection, opt-in nightly
    pg_dump backup.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 23 Aug 2026 02:00:00 -0500
